    {
      "id": "d12dbf78-07b0-471f-96bf-61a535ee5c81",
      "name": "Template description",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -700,
        -200
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 620,
        "height": 900,
        "content": "## Chat with your PDF and Office files, with page citations\n\n**Who's it for:** teams and solo builders who want answers from their own documents (contracts, manuals, reports, slide decks, spreadsheets, scans) with the file and page each answer comes from.\n\n**How it works**\n1. **Add documents** is a form: paste links to PDF, DOCX, PPTX, XLSX, HTML, EPUB or image files.\n2. **Convert to Markdown** runs the Apify Actor *Document to Markdown*. It keeps headings and tables (also borderless PDF tables), reads scanned pages with OCR, and returns heading-aware chunks with page numbers.\n3. **Store chunks** embeds each chunk with OpenAI and saves it in a vector store, with file, title, page and heading as metadata.\n4. **Chat with your documents** opens a chat. The **AI agent** searches the store, answers only from what it finds and cites (title, p. N).\n\n**How to set up**\n1. Create a free Apify account and copy your API token (Apify Console \u2192 Settings \u2192 API & Integrations).\n2. In **Convert to Markdown**, create a *Header Auth* credential: name `Authorization`, value `Bearer YOUR_APIFY_TOKEN`.\n3. Add your OpenAI credential to the two embeddings nodes and the chat model.\n4. Click **Execute workflow** to open the form, paste a few file links and submit. When the run finishes, click **Open chat** and ask a question.\n\n**Requirements:** Apify account ($2 per 1,000 pages, $5 per 1,000 OCR pages) and an OpenAI API key (embeddings cost a few cents per 1,000 pages).\n\n**How to customize**\n- The Simple Vector Store lives in n8n's memory and is cleared on restart. For production, swap both vector store nodes for Pinecone, Qdrant, Supabase or Postgres (PGVector) with the same embeddings.\n- Feed files from Google Drive, Dropbox or S3 with a pre-signed link instead of the form.\n- Change the chunk size in **Configure**. Keep chunk size plus overlap under 1,000 characters, or the loader splits the chunks again."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
